# Cascaded inference routing rules.
#
# This file is intentionally a tiny custom syntax, not YAML.
#
# Terminology:
#   A rule is one routing instruction.
#   The selector is the left side of a rule. It describes which requested
#   provider/model calls the rule matches.
#   The override is the right side of a rule. It describes which provider/model
#   should actually be used when the selector matches.
#   A variant is a provider-local model option. Variant names only have meaning
#   inside one concrete provider and one concrete model.
#
# Rule syntax:
#   selector = override
#   selector = override prefer dimension:weight,dimension:weight
#
# Later matching rules override earlier matching rules.
#
# References:
#   provider>model
#   provider>model@variant
#   provider>model>variant
#
# To specify a variant, both provider and model must be concrete names.
# This applies on both sides of the rule. For example:
#   deepseek>deepseek-v4-pro@fast
# is valid syntax, but:
#   *>deepseek-v4-pro@fast
# is invalid because the provider is wildcarded.
#
# Wildcards:
#   *             matches all providers and all models
#   **            same as *
#   *>*           same as *
#   provider>*    all models from one provider
#   *>model       one model from all providers
#   *model        shorthand for *>model
#
# Groups:
#   Groups are defined in inference-model-groups.rules and referenced with $.
#   Group references can be used with &, |, !, and parentheses:
#     *>($weak-model & !$cheap-model) = crofai>$strong-model
#   _same helpers match parts of the originally requested target.
#   Add ! before any condition to negate it:
#     _same        the exact same provider/model/variant
#     *>_same      the same canonical model
#     _same>*      the same provider
#     !_same       negated version of the same check
#     * = *>($reliable-model & !_same)
#
# Preferences:
#   Use prefer when an override can match multiple choices.
#   Preference dimensions are defined in inference-model-scores.yaml.
#   Use either all weighted or all unweighted dimensions in one prefer clause:
#     * = *>($reliable-model) prefer reliability:70,intelligence:30
#     * = *>($fast-model) prefer speed,price
#
# Override examples:
#   crofai>kimi-k2.6 = deepseek>deepseek-v4-pro
#   *>deepseek-v4-pro = deepseek>deepseek-v4-pro
#   *>old-model = *>new-model
#   * = deepseek>deepseek-v4-pro
#   * = *>($reliable-model & !_same) prefer reliability:50,intelligence:30,price:20
#
# Comments start with # anywhere on a line. Empty and whitespace-only lines are ignored.

# No active provider substitutions. Flows select Command Code directly.
